Answers are graded automatically by running them, so the task must be a program that reads standard input and prints to standard output. Describe the exact stdin layout in input_format and the exact stdout layout in output_format. List the input bounds in constraints (and in the question text), cover the edge cases the recruiter asked for, and include sample input/output inside the question text.
Provide test_cases: at least 3 visible examples (hidden=false) and at least 5 hidden tests (hidden=true) covering edge cases (empty/minimal input, duplicates, large values, ties, and any edge cases the prompts name). Each test is {"input": exact stdin text, "expected_output": exact stdout text, "hidden": bool}.
correct_answer must be a complete Python 3 reference program that reads stdin and prints exactly expected_output for every test (it is used to verify the tests, whatever the candidate language). Leave starter_code empty; per-language templates are supplied.
evaluation_focus lists what the grader should reward (correctness, edge cases, complexity, code quality, or criteria from the prompts).
